{
 "source": "MadLoop/MG5_aMC 3.7.0 standalone exports of tools/loop_reference/required_processes.json (gt_tttx_ew, gb_ttxb_ew_mb; loop_qcd_qed_sm_Gmu, 't Hooft-Feynman gauge, real on-shell masses, widths zero), the Born x CT interference split by tools/loop_reference/madloop_ct_selection.py",
 "provenance": {
  "references": "reference/runs/required/<name>/reference.json of the workspace (tools/loop_reference/madloop_export.py and run_required.sh <name> madloop): Born and full virtual; points and scales are the reference's",
  "components": "tools/loop_reference/madloop_ct_selection.py --work reference/runs/required/<name> --orders 2 4 2 6 --alpha-s 0.118 --group 'mixing=C_UV(G0Z|AG0|GPWM|GMWP)MASS' --group 'r2=\\bR2_' (gt_tttx_ew), --group 'neutral=C_UV(G0Z|AG0)MASS' --group 'charged=C_UV(GPWM|GMWP)MASS' --group 'r2=\\bR2_' (gb_ttxb_ew_mb): the generated SKIPLOOPEVAL switch and a selection of CT interference indices in a copy of loop_matrix.f, the export unchanged; ct = every CT amplitude, r2 = the amplitudes with an R2 coupling, mixing/neutral/charged = the Goldstone-vector mixing counterterms V_UVG0ZMassEW, V_UVAG0MassEW, V_UVGpWmMassEW, V_UVGmWpMassEW; r2_g0tt and omitted_r2 (gt_tttx_ew): the same tool with --group 'G0TT=\\bR2_G0TT\\b' --group 'G0TT_B=\\bR2_G0TT_B\\b' --group 'HTT=\\bR2_HTT\\b' --group 'HTT_B=\\bR2_HTT_B\\b' --group 'r2=\\bR2_(?!(G0TT|G0TT_B|HTT|HTT_B)\\b)' (ct and the R2 groups' sum equal the components above; R2_G0TT_B selects no amplitude)",
  "ttx_ttx_ew": "required/ttx_ttx_ew.json (MadLoop and Recola); components: tools/loop_reference/madloop_ct_selection.py --work reference/runs/required/ttx_ttx_ew --orders 0 4 0 6 --alpha-s 0.118 --group 'r2=\\bR2_' --group 'mixing=C_UV(G0Z|AG0|GPWM|GMWP)MASS'; the export's helas_calls_ampb_1.f calls R2_G0TT, R2_HTT and R2_HTT_B 4 times each and R2_G0TT_B never",
  "ttx_zh_ew": "required/ttx_zh_ew.json (MadLoop and Recola); components: tools/loop_reference/madloop_ct_selection.py --work reference/runs/required/ttx_zh_ew --orders 0 4 0 6 --alpha-s 0.118 --group 'r2=\\bR2_' --group 'mixing=C_UV(G0Z|AG0|GPWM|GMWP)MASS'; the export's helas_calls_ampb_1.f calls R2_G0TT once, R2_HTT and R2_HTT_B twice each and R2_G0TT_B never"
 },
 "scope": "Correctness references only, MadLoop in double precision (return code 110 for the CT selections). The UV counterterm component (ct - r2, the mixings included) is the oracle of the Goldstone-vector mixings' sign (WP3.2 EWI-7b): the mixings make 0.3 to 3 % of it in gt_tttx_ew and 150 % at point 0 of gb_ttxb_ew_mb, which pyAmpliCol does not generate yet (an EW ghost vertex read through no conjugate rule). In gt_tttx_ew the bare part (virtual - ct) and the whole virtual are oracles too, with MadLoop's omitted R2_G0tt_b added (omitted_r2, r2_g0tt).",
 "convention": "MadLoop/BLHA C_eps=(4pi)^eps/Gamma(1-eps); F_MadLoop=F_Recola+pi^2/6*D; OpenLoops truepoles=1, polenorm=0; physical couplings, no alpha extraction; initial spin/colour average and final identical-particle factor included",
